# Public names the symbol stream does not carry.
#
# `axiom symbols` has no arm for `TAG_D_MACRO` and none for
# `TAG_D_IMPL`, and its `TAG_D_EFFECT` arm registers the effect's
# OPERATIONS rather than the effect itself (`self_host/symbols.ax`,
# the declaration dispatch). So these thirteen names are public API
# that `scripts/check-compat.sh` cannot see - twelve macros, among
# them `println` and `format`, and one effect declaration.
#
# This is a hole in the contract and it is written down rather than
# left to be discovered. It is compared as a SET, not a count: a
# fourteenth invisible name fails the gate, and closing the hole is
# this file becoming empty.
#
# CLOSED 2026-08-26. `symbols.ax` gained a `TAG_D_MACRO` arm and an
# arm recording an `(effect ...)` declaration's own name, so all 420
# public names now carry a row and this list is empty.
#
# It stays, and it stays COMPARED. The gate reads it as a SET, so an
# empty file is the assertion that nothing has left the stream - a
# fourteenth invisible name would fail here, which is exactly the
# check that was missing when twelve macros were outside the contract
# and nothing said so.
